  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "You’d like to better understand how your regression model improves with more training. The loop in this program trains a new network four times, allowing it 1, 10, 100 and then 1000 passes over the drives, and prints each network’s prediction for drive 1.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Predict what happens to the prediction for drive 1 as `max_iter` grows from 1 to 1000.\r\n- Run the program to test your prediction.\r\n- Study the four printed predictions. At which `max_iter` do the predictions stop changing as much?\r\n- Run the program again. Be ready to share what you notice: which numbers changed, and which stayed the same?\r\n",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "true",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
